3. Third-party components

Versions of Smart Trader up to and including 1.23.0 contained components of other authors under the MIT License and
the Apache License 2.0. None of their code is in Smart Trader after 1.23.0: clean-room rewrites replaced it. They are
listed with their copyright lines, the versions that held them and their full licence texts in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. In those versions each of them stays under its own licence, and nothing in this notice limits
the rights those licences give or adds restrictions they do not allow.
Smart Trader also contains short wordings from Team Fortress 2's own localization files by Valve Corporation (item and
attribute names in English, Ukrainian and Russian, and the names of Unusual effects: src/data/tf2-words.js,
src/data/tf2-particles.js), used only to recognise the texts Steam's own pages show. They are Valve's; this notice
grants nothing for them, and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md names them with their sources.

